node 2_20260821-201403 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this convolution kernel, I identified that it's **structurally direct**: while it stages weights into shared memory, the input activations are read directly from global memory with no reuse across threads despite significant receptive-field overlap (K=3, stride=1), and the accumulation is dominated by nested scalar loops. This matches the "structurally direct" criteria, so I'll perform a **structural rewrite**: CTA-level 3D spatial output tiling combined with shared-memory staging of the input tile (with zero-padding baked in), eliminating redundant global memory loads and per-element bounds checks during the compute loop, while keeping the existing weight shared-memory staging and output-channel register blocking.

