The most impactful single optimization here is to **rebalance the channel-tile size (CcPerBlock) to reduce register pressure and improve occupancy** while preserving the same cooperative tiled/shared-memory structure. Reducing `CcPerBlock` from 64 to 32 halves the per-thread accumulator registers (64 instead of 128), roughly halves per-block shared memory for the weight tile, and doubles the number of channel-tile blocks along `grid.y`, giving the scheduler more independent blocks per SM to fill the pipeline and hide latency — all without changing the convolution semantics or algorithmic structure.

