node 9_20260821-224032 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this kernel, it's a **(C) Convolution kernel** that is already cooperative and tiled — it uses CTA-level output tiling, shared-memory staging for both weights and input patches, and per-thread accumulation with compile-time unrolled loops (CIN/KH/KW as template constants) for the specialized "cached" kernel path (which is what gets dispatched for the given Cin=3, K=3 test case).

Since the kernel is already tiled/cooperative, I'll apply **register blocking**: currently, inside the specialized kernel's inner accumulation loop, the weight value `sW(oc, ic, kh, kw)` is re-read from shared memory on every iteration of the outer `od` (Dout) loop, even though the weight doesn't depend on `od` at all. This causes `Dout`-times redundant shared-memory reads per output channel. I hoist these weight loads into a small register array (`Wreg[CIN][KH][KW]`, fully unrolled at compile time since CIN/KH/KW are compile-time constants) computed once per output channel `oc`, before the `od` loop, eliminating redundant shared memory traffic and reducing pressure on the LSU/shared-memory pipeline while keeping compute in registers.

