node 1_20260821-224948 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this convolution kernel, I identify it as **(C) Convolution kernel**. The current implementation is structurally direct: each thread reloads input activations (`mX(cin, ih, iw)`) directly from global memory for every output pixel it computes, even though neighboring output pixels within a tile heavily overlap in their receptive fields (kernel is 5x9 with dilation (2,3), giving effective receptive field 9x25). Only the weight is staged in shared memory; the input tile — which has the most reuse potential — is not staged at all.

I apply a **structural rewrite**: CTA-level 2D spatial output tiling with shared-memory staging of the reusable input tile per input channel, so all threads in a block cooperatively load an input patch once per `cin` and reuse it across the whole output tile and all output channels in the block, eliminating redundant global memory reads of overlapping input regions.

