node 9_20260822-011547 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this flash-attention kernel, it already implements shared-memory tiling, vectorized loads, and bank-conflict-reduced permutation. However, K/V tile loading and compute are strictly serialized (`load → syncthreads → compute → syncthreads`), with no overlap between global-memory latency and arithmetic work. I apply **software-pipelined double buffering**: while computing on the current K/V tile (from shared-memory buffer A), the next tile is concurrently prefetched into buffer B, hiding global memory latency behind compute.

